  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "natural_late_bodies",
      "status": "supported_for_declared_fixture",
      "detail": "The natural fixed-native endpoint visibly contains all ten scaffolded construction bodies, not ten pending foundations. Linden, Wren, Meadowsweet, Sorrel, Tamar, Rook, Hart, Sain, Bracken, and Hare are all present. In particular Sain, Bracken, and Hare are rendered where the older C1/C2 late captures lacked one or more bodies. The natural day/night repeat and restored images retain all ten bodies. No obvious hard clipping, detached major construction body, or absent last-site building was observed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cold_state_preserved",
      "status": "observed",
      "detail": "Both natural cold draw PNGs retain ten plain foundation/pending plots. The explicit-flush cold pair and the after-flush-before-render PNG also show the same ten plots. The post-flush-before-render image is not itself evidence that construction bodies were drawn."
    },
    {
      "id": "natural_readiness_timing",
      "status": "ci_record_with_visual_endpoint_support",
      "detail": "The natural route records zero flush calls and exactly twelve native observations/frame delta twelve, with a reported observation interval of 524.2 ms. Its pending sequence is 10,9,7,6,5,4,3,0,0,0,0,0. Thus the first recorded zero-pending point is observation 8; observation 12 is the predeclared fixed endpoint, not the first readiness instant. The endpoint has ten sites, zero pending, zero shell misses, and zero Layer A misses. Timing is this CI fixture only, not a startup-performance promise."
    },
    {
      "id": "explicit_flush_diagnostic",
      "status": "separate_diagnostic_only",
      "detail": "The separately labelled explicit-flush route also visibly renders all ten bodies at its sixty-six-observation endpoint. CI records exactly one native flush call. Its roofs/cranes/construction appearance differ in some details from the natural endpoint, so no cross-route pixel-equivalence claim is made. This route is diagnostic and must not be presented as ordinary cold-start evidence."
    },
    {
      "id": "repeat_and_negative",
      "status": "supported_with_provenance_split",
      "detail": "Read-only full-PNG decoding independently confirms each natural/explicit route day/night repeat pair and its restored image are exactly identical across all 3,363,840 RGBA bytes. The real-canvas one-pixel corruption rejection and withheld-readiness rejection are reported by the official CI manifest; this reviewer did not recreate those browser negative controls locally."
    },
    {
      "id": "occlusion_limits",
      "status": "retained",
      "detail": "Scaffolds, cranes, front facades, and roofs occlude fine joins. This evidence establishes presence of ten late-stage bodies in rotation 0, but does not reveal Hare corridor endpoints hidden by its roofs, rear bracket joins, or complete hidden construction topology. Tamar retains the native silhouette construction shell rather than a finished bare roof. No claim is made that these captures reveal every architectural detail."
    }
  ],
